I don't think these will be normalized. Looking at the definition of `FLOAT_ARRAY_RANDOM_FUNC`, its

```
float[] fa = new float[size];
        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {
            fa[i] = randomFloat();
        }
        return fa;
```
And that can easily result in a non-normalized vector. 

I think there will need to be a new function that generates a vector like `FLOAT_ARRAY_RANDOM_FUNC`, but then takes the l2Norm of it.
